<https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKPlatformTerminology#SocioTechnicalSystems>
        a       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created>
                "20/04/2022" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator>
                "Lucy McKenna" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition>
                "The term STS was coined by Trist and colleagues in the Tavistock Institute in London in the 1950s and later taken up by Klein to recognise the interaction between technical and social factors in organisations. When trying to change a system STS would stress the need to consider the technical and social factors and the impact of the change on other aspects of the system." ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme>
                <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKPlatformTerminology#> ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel>
                "Socio-technical systems (STS)" .

